---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro'
import { LINKS, SITE } from '../../consts'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this website collects, what a self-hosted Playarr server does with your data, and what the hosted Playarr linking service briefly holds."
>
  <Section eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        Three separate things are worth keeping apart: this website, the server you run yourself,
        and the hosted Playarr service.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a set of static pages. It sets no tracking cookies, runs no analytics, embeds
        no third-party scripts, and has no forms to submit. The single piece of state it keeps is
        your light or dark theme preference, stored in your own browser and never transmitted
        anywhere.
      </p>
      <p>
        Whoever hosts these pages will keep ordinary web-server request logs, as any web server
        does.
      </p>

      <h2>The server you run</h2>
      <p>
        A {SITE.name} server is yours. Your library, your accounts, your watch history and your
        artwork cache live on your own storage, under your own control. The project operates no
        service that this data is sent to.
      </p>
      <p>
        The server does reach out to the library-management applications and metadata sources you
        configure it to reach, that is the point of configuring them, and it fetches artwork from
        the URLs those applications provide, caching it locally.
      </p>

      <h2>The hosted Playarr service</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={LINKS.playarrApp} rel="noopener">playarr.app</a> hosts the Playarr web application
        and can broker the first handshake between a new app and a server it has not met. That is
        the one moment something passes through infrastructure the project operates.
      </p>
      <p>The short-lived link record contains only:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the device secret generated by the app,</li>
        <li>the server addresses you chose, and</li>
        <li>a single-use device code.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        It never contains a password, a browser bearer token, or a refresh token, and it expires
        within minutes. After linking, the app talks to your server directly and nothing further
        routes through the hosted service.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If any of the above changes, particularly if analytics are ever added to this site, or the
        hosted service ever holds more than it does today, this page will be updated to say so
        before the change ships.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: var(--width-prose);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }

  .prose ul {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    padding-inline-start: 1.35em;
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
</style>
